# MDC Rule: WordPress Theme Development Best Practices

- Use child themes for customizations instead of modifying parent themes directly.
- Enqueue styles and scripts using wp_enqueue_style() and wp_enqueue_script().
- Use template hierarchy and template parts for maintainable theme structure.
- Make themes translation-ready using WordPress internationalization functions and load text domains.
- Follow accessibility best practices (WCAG 2.1 AA) for all user-facing features.
- Use the Customizer API for theme options.
- Use modern JavaScript (ES6+) and build tools for asset management; enqueue minified and versioned assets.
- Include proper theme headers for WordPress recognition.
- Test themes with the latest version of WordPress and major browsers.

## Examples

```php
// Accessibility
<label for="user_email"><?php esc_html_e( 'Email Address', 'my-theme' ); ?></label>
<input type="email" id="user_email" name="user_email" aria-required="true" />
```

```php
// Asset management
enqueue_script(
    'my-theme-main',
    get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/js/main.min.js',
    array( 'jquery' ),
    '1.0.0',
    true
);
```

```php
// Theme header
/*
Theme Name: My Theme
Description: Example theme.
Version: 1.0.0
Author: Your Name
Text Domain: my-theme
*/
```

This rule applies to all *.php files in all subdirectories.







